        synopsis {get_bels ?-regexp? ?-nocase? ?-filter expression? ?-of_objects objects? ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?patterns?}
        description {Basic Elements, or BELs, are the building blocks of logic such as flip-flops, LUTs and carry logic that make up a SLICE. This command returns the BELs on the target part matching a search pattern in an open design; the default pattern is the wildcard * which gets all BELs on the device. Like every get_ command it returns a container list of a single type of object, and only objects of that type may be appended to it.}
        returns {A list of BEL objects.}
        example {llength [get_bels]}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2012.2}
    }
}
