        synopsis {remove_cell cells ... ?-quiet? ?-verbose?}
        description {Removes cells from the current netlist in either an open Synthesized or Implemented design, where an instance name can be given hierarchically from the top-level using the hierarchy separator character. Netlist editing changes the in-memory view of the netlist only; changes may be saved with write_checkpoint or exported with the appropriate write_* command. Netlist editing is not allowed on an RTL design.}
        returns {Nothing.}
        example {remove_cell fftEngine
remove_cell usbEngine0/usb_out}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2012.2}
    }
}
