        summary {Report pulse width checks.}
        synopsis {report_pulse_width ?-file file? ?-append? ?-name name? ?-return_string? ?-all_violators? ?-significant_digits digits? ?-limit count? ?-min_period? ?-max_period? ?-low_pulse? ?-high_pulse? ?-max_skew? ?-clocks clocks? ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?objects?}
        description {Reports the pulse width of the specified clock signals in the clock network and upon reaching the flip-flop, performing high pulse width checking with maximum delay for the rising edge and minimum delay for the falling edge, and low pulse width checking with minimum delay for the rising edge and maximum delay for the falling edge, so that the result is a worst case analysis of the current synthesized or implemented design. The report includes minimum period, maximum period, low pulse width, and high pulse width checks by default, but selecting a specific check disables the others unless they are also specified. The report is returned to the standard output unless -file, -return_string, or -name is specified.}
        returns {Nothing.}
        example {report_pulse_width -min_period -low_pulse -name timing_1}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2012.2}
    }
}
