        synopsis {startgroup ?-try? ?-quiet? ?-verbose?}
        description {Starts a sequence of commands that can be undone or redone as a series, ended by the endgroup command. You can have multiple command groups to undo or redo, but command groups cannot be nested, so an open sequence must be closed with endgroup before a new startgroup.}
        returns {Int: 1 when startgroup has started a new group, 0 when a group is already started.}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2012.2}
    }
}
