        summary {Undo the previous command.}
        synopsis {undo ?-list? ?-quiet? ?-verbose?}
        description {Undoes a prior command, and can be used repeatedly to undo a series of commands. When a group of commands has been created with startgroup and endgroup, the command undoes that group as a sequence, starting at the endgroup and continuing until it reaches the startgroup. An undone command can be reapplied with redo.}
        returns {With -list, the list of undoable tasks.}
        example {undo -list}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2012.2}
    }
}
